// The six factions of the Venus cloud deck as diplomacy SIDES.
//
// Declared from //shared/signal/create_sides in __init__.mast, the route LM declares its own
// sides from, so they exist before player ships and before any map runs.
//
// A side is not the faction name on a hull. shipData `side`/`origin` says what a ship IS
// (how a prefab finds "a Syndicate cruiser"); THIS file says who shoots whom. They share
// names because that reads better.
//
// Relations are declared from BOTH ends on purpose: the engine's table is directional, and
// LM's own sides.amd carries the same duplication with a warning not to tidy it up.
//
// THE SHAPE OF THE WAR: the Iron Syndicate raids everyone who builds; the Brood is a
// hunger, not a nation, and everyone fights it; the Flotilla trades with all but the Brood.
// A mission that wants a different war flips sides at runtime with side_set_relations.

# [Salvage Flotilla](flotilla)
---
Color: #DA4
Enemies: brood
---
Riverboat salvagers on wrecked starship hulls. They trade with anyone who will moor.

# [Aurelian Concord](concord)
---
Color: #EEC
Enemies: syndicate, brood
---
A luxury zeppelin navy rebuilt from chrome ocean-liner starships.

# [Atomic Directorate](directorate)
---
Color: #E44
Enemies: syndicate, brood
---
Finned rocket ships of a nation that tamed the atom; every lift ring orbits a reactor.

# [Iron Syndicate](syndicate)
---
Color: #8A4
Enemies: concord, directorate, commons, brood
---
Armored warships of a militarist world. They take what the others build.

# [Sunward Commons](commons)
---
Color: #7C5
Enemies: syndicate, brood
---
Garden-grown eco-starships on solar-sail wings. They would rather grow than fight.

# [Verdant Brood](brood)
---
Color: #A4E
Enemies: flotilla, concord, directorate, syndicate, commons
---
Living bio-starships regrown into flying creatures. A hunger, not a nation.

# [Venus](venus)
---
Color: #CB8
---
The cloud deck itself: weather, resource clouds and wrecks. Nobody's side.
